ent axon and establishment of neuronal polarity. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>14</volume>:<fpage>2025</fpage>&#x02013;2032.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15556865</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">Wang, H.R., Y. Zhang, B. Ozdamar, A.A. Ogunjimi, E. Alexandrova, G.H. Thomsen, and J.L. Wrana. <year>2003</year>. Regulation of cell polarity and protrusion formation by targeting RhoA for degradation. <source>Science.</source> <volume>302</volume>:<fpage>1775</fpage>&#x02013;1779.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14657501</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><citation citation-type="journal">Yoshimura, T., Y. Kawano, N. Arimura, S. Kawabata, A. Kikuchi, and K. Kaibuchi. <year>2005</year>. GSK-3beta regulates phosphorylation of CRMP-2 and neuronal polarity. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>120</volume>:<fpage>137</fpage>&#x02013;149.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15652488</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><citation citation-type="journal">Zheng, J.Q., M. Felder, J.A. Connor, and M.M. Poo. <year>1994</year>. Turning of nerve growth cones induced by neurotransmitters. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>368</volume>:<fpage>140</fpage>&#x02013;144.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8139655</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>